      "content": "it just feels like a loop. i try to think about \"something new\" but my brain just goes to the same place. it's just a constant, hollow ache. like i'm just waiting for a clock to run out, but even that feels like too much effort. does it ever actually get better, or do people just get better at pretending everything isn't completely empty?",
